    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000091302,
      "SummaryText": "Executive Summary of Risk Management Plan for:\nUnited Ethanol, LLC\nMilton, WI\n\nINTRODUCTION:\nUnited Ethanol, LLC (United Ethanol) has constructed and is operating a fuel grade ethanol production facility in Milton, Wisconsin.  It produces fuel-grade ethanol from corn through a fermentation process.  The spent grains, or Distillers Dried Grains and Solubles, is sold as animal feed and a portion of the carbon dioxide generated during fermentation also recovered and sold.\n\nUnited Ethanol, LLC is required by law to denature its ethanol product prior to shipment.  A liquid petroleum based blend is used which includes three regulated flammable substances; pentane, isopentane and butane.  The denaturant is stored in an outdoor, 2,031 barrel (85,000 gallon) storage tank surrounded by a foot high secondary containment dike. \nDenaturant is also present in rail tanker cars that have been loaded with blended ethanol and denaturant awaiting shipment by the rail carrier.\n\nRELEASE PREVENTION RESPONSE POLICY\nUnited Ethanol, LLC is committed to managing the facility in accordance with relevant regulations and good manufacturing practices to minimize the risk of an accidental release of a regulated substance from the storage tank and loading process. If an accidental release was to occur, United Ethanol, LLC has response measures in place to minimize the impact of the release.  \n\nFIVE YEAR ACCIDENT HISTORY\nNo accidental release has occurred in the past five years.\n\nEMERGENCY RESPONSE PLAN AND EMERGENCY ACTION PLAN\nUnited Ethanol, LLC has developed an emergency response plan and an emergency action plan that provides procedures for:\n\n(1)\tInforming the public and local emergency response agencies about an accidental release;\n(2)\tFirst aid and emergency medical treatment for employees;\n(3)\tEmergency response after an accidental release of a regulated substance;\n(4)\tThe availability of emergency response equipment and its inspection, testing and maintenance;\n(5)\tTraining all employees in"
    },
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 1,
      "FacilityID": 1000091302,
      "SummaryText": "relevant procedures; and\n(6)\tEmergency response plan review and update.\n\nUnited Ethanol, LLC employees receive emergency response training annually.  In the event of an emergency, United Ethanol, LLC has a  notification system for notifying facility personnel.  During an environmental release accident, the shift supervisor is responsible for implementing the chemical release procedure as outlined in the Emergency Response Plan.  In addition, the plant manager is responsible for public notification.\n\nCHANGES TO SAFETY\nUnited Ethanol, LLC developed a set of procedures, as part of the Management of Change system, to identify and determine if major modifications are conducted properly, and to ensure that employees are notified about and understand the ramifications of these changes. \n\nINTEGRITY\nUnited Ethanol, LLC has completed its 10-year non-destructive testing for all of its Process Safety Management (PSM) system requirements."
    }
  ]
